{%- comment -%}
  Besjaar 11.7.3 — mobile menu category rows.

  The two collection links under CATEGORIEEN rendered as bordered pill cards
  (besjaar-mobile-corrections.css gives them a border, a radius and a tinted
  background) while every sibling row in the same list — Keuzehulp, Over ons,
  Reviews, FAQ — is a plain full-width link with a hairline under it. Same
  list, two different controls, which is what the difference looked like.

  They now use the sibling treatment. Carried as a header-group section rather
  than an asset because a section renders in the body, after every stylesheet
  in the head, so it lands on top of the pill rules without an !important war
  or a load-order change.
  2026-09-13 consolidation: this section's <style> block was extracted during
  the CSS bundling pass. The rules above are now served from
  assets/besjaar-seo-carriers-late.css, loaded by besjaar-desktop-fixes-1170.
  Editing this file changes nothing — edit the bundle instead. The section is
  kept so existing header-group settings stay valid.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Besjaar menu rows",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "11.7.3: makes the two category links in the mobile menu match the other menu rows instead of rendering as bordered cards. Keep in the header group."
    }
  ],
  "enabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
